{"posts":[{"id":"dbrrbd_p2_26","t":"whiteout wrote: When looks messy, go on LTF Looks how different are the same messy on m30, and i have designed the zone approximately ecouse you have to do precisely:cheer: ]. Still a mess? Go on m15, then down.\n\nHey Whiteout, Question about your chart, the second rectangle, isn't that just a reaction from the 1st RBD-zone? Regards,","a":"xmzhang","d":"","n":"#26","p":2,"im":["ed3a4a1b489c4e1f6a6479c1903318dde379dc6a"],"m":26},{"id":"dbrrbd_p2_27","t":"hy X\n\nsorry, which one? Anyway their are draw very approximately just to show the concept...but if you are talking about the rectangle around 11 jul, nope, is drew approximatly but is there for a reason, check on ltf.","a":"whiteout","d":"","n":"#27","p":2,"im":[],"m":27},{"id":"dbrrbd_p2_28","t":"Here are my charts 1-4 of my homework. Your feedback is more than welcome\n\nLes_Paul","a":"Les_Paul","d":"","n":"#28","p":2,"im":["5a47f4cb471f27ef33f084567c330def27365f67","d18bbe5d5ea6bc9f77d708aa4e1191e1e0be945f","d87b365608773734eea44b735e266b1d8657e4aa","38651421c1e3c901b244a6fe68109eb43ae274a6"],"m":28},{"id":"dbrrbd_p2_29","t":"Lovely work, L_P.\n\nI'm glad you're adding other stuff that you see too","a":"Ifmyante","d":"","n":"#29","p":2,"im":[],"m":29},{"id":"dbrrbd_p2_30","t":"minimalmonk wrote: yes it happened here. i remember that i've read on PIE or PIE chat something about this. eg. demand just slice supply zone. movement up is quick and strong and some orders in movement direction remain unfilled, so resistance become support till next time. is the truth in it?\n\nyes. that's the guideline; as always you ll watch price approaching, confluence, and the other stuff..just don't push the trigger on all the ignored resistence.","a":"whiteout","d":"","n":"#30","p":2,"im":[],"m":30},{"id":"dbrrbd_p2_31","t":"Just marked up some examples from the EURUSD chart. Most of these worked out, but I added a couple that didn't in lower TFs too.\n\nThink I may add another chart shortly just focusing on those setups that didn't work and how price reacted on its return.\n\nAs always, any feedback is welcome:cheer:","a":"Ezabo","d":"","n":"#31","p":2,"im":["41644df53e100e0fb6f824edee90e6b76a2696bd"],"m":31},{"id":"dbrrbd_p2_32","t":"I started my DBR/RBD homework analysing daily audusd. When there were a very specific decision point I marked it with a red line, that when is on the outside part of the zone, it could be considered also as a Support or Resistance line. It is, and it is also the outside border of the SD zone. Other times, this red line is exactly the point where the decision was made (when the base is broken by the long candle)","a":"okami","d":"","n":"#32","p":2,"im":["4c9538a5b87233ccf8080d97ea9e2ecbbde37fda","38b2be705d922ac054cacad646d3f63c70a7a98f"],"m":32},{"id":"dbrrbd_p2_33","t":"A 5M eu analysis","a":"okami","d":"","n":"#33","p":2,"im":["c889492bed1663406acae8fa7c9e175629c5fc58"],"m":33},{"id":"dbrrbd_p2_34","t":"A complete eu analysis from Monthly to 1H\n\nMontly Chart\n\nThe same montly chart, but signaling the rejections to decision points:\n\nIsn't that a QM? (yet to do the HW, though):\n\neurusd Weekly:\n\neurusd Daily:\n\neu 4H:\n\neu 1H:\n\nSo, broken the 1H demand, should we expect a rejection in 1.21-1.20 in the Weekly Demand?...","a":"okami","d":"","n":"#34","p":2,"im":["2d764e9b7710c6ad775c61260f44aa9ddbe6cd6b","40d3153c0a522817e28f50c252962f1d304ae077","6604ee4f8f9631090683e4f4babf755133ef5961","96f35473169cd0ee0b4704180b2347c279a26fda","c3dd8553a61cc0eea9872add33f699b28659ead3","3e865bf7407c25dd30521058b637ae066fa68582","038ad1b8d63bc756d684e986b41a6fb2c3621a75"],"m":34},{"id":"dbrrbd_p2_35","t":"And just for fun, cable analysis in 70 and 1 ticks","a":"okami","d":"","n":"#35","p":2,"im":["c6c5740dbb4ef2f9c0dd595903abc0007356d5d1","d28a8cac403a47d0985477ccd9c6ec195a5a7136"],"m":35},{"id":"dbrrbd_p2_36","t":"DBR and RBD\n\nYellow squares are s/d ignored and reacted on its way to the area. Black lines are S/R","a":"Osman","d":"","n":"#36","p":2,"im":["29e0c715a66a8a4b015a451b7e74a33fd4c2362e"],"m":36},{"id":"dbrrbd_p2_37","t":"EUR 4hr\n\nIn this chart ive marked only the DRB/RBD that were able to make a higher high/lower low than the previous swing.","a":"Osman","d":"","n":"#37","p":2,"im":["1d7a4b8e97966f8cc71b6e123b8c206651f008f7"],"m":37},{"id":"dbrrbd_p2_38","t":"Good work Osman\n\nI'd really like to be able to better judge your understanding of these levels, so I have 2 requests for you-\n\n1. please draw your boxes as far right as is relevant - over time you'll get some surprises about how relevant these zones can be over time\n\n2. give some on-chart explanations about what you notice\n\nThanks, and keep it up\n\nIf","a":"Ifmyante","d":"","n":"#38","p":2,"im":[],"m":38},{"id":"dbrrbd_p2_39","t":"Sure, ill do so.\n\nThx!","a":"Osman","d":"","n":"#39","p":2,"im":[],"m":39},{"id":"dbrrbd_p2_40","t":"Hey Guys,\n\nI have marked S&D zones on current AUDUSD H1 chart as a part of my homework. I have also included few comments. I'm looking for a sell signals (smaller TF) on this pair until the daily demand is reached.\n\nAny comments and critique is most welcome.\n\nCheers Elin","a":"Elin","d":"","n":"#40","p":2,"im":[],"m":40},{"id":"dbrrbd_p2_41","t":"Chokdee\n\nI'm not sure if some of my RBD/DBR have enough base to them, making them more like RD's and DR's. Although, on the next time-frame down the base is present. Any comments are more than welcome! Thanks, Chokdee","a":"—","d":"","n":"#41","p":2,"im":["a287356918eaab92058f689a44503e27409feada","732a5665d0f5e08f4212c025ea99322ccbaf1dd1","86997ab56dd441cf333885f3ca8c08c61e31ada0","8e033efce2999000865d901d0d2c02fcc2023df9"],"m":41},{"id":"dbrrbd_p2_42","t":"hi chokdee yes, when looks a little mess go into LTF...and a DBR / RBD could have a little base, rally into S zones then price falls down immidiatly - nice!! a lot of supply - but generally speaking you can find quite always a little base on ltf, and you will love that base. ttle retracemente to the base..and puf you go short..if trade a lot this way.] just 2 hints try to drawn that zone more accuratly tart an homework session on an h1 m30 or m15 so can have more hystory to scan than the W1] pay attention to the difference between RBD/DBR and RBR/DBD they are both decision point and you have to pay attention to both, but they are different [of course a D1 RBR will contain a lot of RBD and DBR and RBR/DBR in the LFT]. must have some scheme at home, i will post later.","a":"whiteout","d":"","n":"#42","p":2,"im":[],"m":42},{"id":"dbrrbd_p2_43","t":"Here goes...","a":"FX.Sniffer","d":"","n":"#43","p":2,"im":["a8e1447edbeba38a17e541a01c55ad3253071868"],"m":43},{"id":"dbrrbd_p2_44","t":"Hi all,\n\nHope I got this right.\n\nAL","a":"AL","d":"","n":"#44","p":2,"im":["b500e0c1c447936995f9078032a7eb686f7d3a0a","0de8209030d0ecbbaab8620fa0bd6af28bd067ae","15cd108d67697ce4cb6551c09449b3a9c54d03d2","53ab98ba0ebd637da71e6dca50291aad888985ef","a0790fc0f1ac99c63137dc2706d3c162656a0424","cd8d8828ab42b3d5c57e195facec5b919fc91122","74b8d3e421b3a6f001a97e6ba3d4458b5def9817","6b36a911829e11d89c25c704835ce3f927951ced"],"m":44},{"id":"dbrrbd_p2_45","t":"Hi al, nice to see that now you can post pictures and charts. ok, about the chart you have posted...yeah you have got the idea, but the aim of the homework is not just spot them and draw some rectangle around them, is to understand that every Rally Base Drop - Drop Base Rally or Rally Base Rally - Drop Base Rally -is a decision point.\n\nThat's why you wonna find that point and then see how price have reacted to that later, becouse we are dealing whit decision point. Like all in life they have a different value, some are big important point other no etc etc.\n\nFind a drop base rally, mark that area, and see what price have done the next time that price have visited that point and so on. hope that make sense. orry for bad eng]\n\nps: in this chart i have roughly marked just some of them, just to give you the idea..i can assure you that after you have spent some time on them you will see some complex story around every one of them.","a":"whiteout","d":"","n":"#45","p":2,"im":["11103f032f738f0e3d5a414ff624718474498eb8"],"m":45},{"id":"dbrrbd_p2_46","t":"Hi Al, Whiteout,\n\nI opened a journal, inspired by this discussion, to further investigate price. This is the link\n\nHere is a chart to also illustrated what whiteout is saying:","a":"okami","d":"","n":"#46","p":2,"im":["f127b89e757bf94537423f2139ac30eb99d7105c"],"m":46},{"id":"dbrrbd_p2_47","t":"Thanks whiteout.\n\nyour comments are noted, and I will examine this closer later on.\n\nAL","a":"AL","d":"","n":"#47","p":2,"im":[],"m":47},{"id":"dbrrbd_p2_48","t":"Hi Okami,\n\nThanks for your input and link to journal. I will definately check this out.\n\nAL","a":"AL","d":"","n":"#48","p":2,"im":[],"m":48},{"id":"dbrrbd_p2_49","t":"","a":"okami","d":"","n":"#49","p":2,"im":["436967cba8ba8cc7f36e642e92956a8b16848340","3d878c9a5a291f60be9773ed2349a1848e4046b6","0a913b91bef679b3720a58a526cf080500151215","d0f0b0f38b92533a7ec1cd2aba2af3ddf400ba21","3fa0834915a6561270e5857f1f6d92fd3e74becf","5aa7102942ed4c4682e587dc63c358dc7a5cf439","9e2e9f314dce0772aee2f2a47b522ad35075514d","64527fd6e0b820d0ec698f2c27a100032004005e"],"m":49},{"id":"dbrrbd_p2_50","t":"This is really great work Okami:cheer:\n\nHas it affected the way you look at price in real time?","a":"Ifmyante","d":"","n":"#50","p":2,"im":[],"m":50}],"images":[{"k":"5a47f4cb471f27ef33f084567c330def27365f67","t":"assets/thumbs/5a47f4cb471f27ef33f084567c330def27365f67.webp","f":"assets/images/5a47f4cb471f27ef33f084567c330def27365f67.png","w":1110,"h":526,"b":42151,"o":"5a47f4cb471f27ef33f084567c330def27365f67.png","p":2,"pid":"dbrrbd_p2_28"},{"k":"d18bbe5d5ea6bc9f77d708aa4e1191e1e0be945f","t":"assets/thumbs/d18bbe5d5ea6bc9f77d708aa4e1191e1e0be945f.webp","f":"assets/images/d18bbe5d5ea6bc9f77d708aa4e1191e1e0be945f.png","w":1356,"h":556,"b":64211,"o":"d18bbe5d5ea6bc9f77d708aa4e1191e1e0be94